\frametitle{The machine re-judges the result}
The FSM measures its own baseline (1{,}346.8 steps/s, gates green),
  receives the fused strip-2 kernel, and issues its own verdict:
  \begin{Verbatim}[frame=single,framesep=1.5mm]
{"exp": 1, "fused": true, "strip": 2, "compile_ok": true,
 "verify_ok": true, "steps_per_sec": 2116.4, "verdict": "keep"}
  \end{Verbatim}
  Then the driver cheats: same kernel, rainfall doubled in one cell update.
  It compiles; the gate fails it; the driver requests \texttt{benchmark} anyway:
  \begin{Verbatim}[frame=single,framesep=1.5mm]
{"error": "invalid_transition", "requested": "benchmark",
 "valid_next_actions": ["log_variant"],
 "message": "action 'benchmark' is not reachable from
             current state."}
  \end{Verbatim}
  The broken variant is ledgered as a revert with a null speed.
